  "aiContextParagraph": "Authorities have brought charges against two men, identified as 34-year-old Mirgen Doku and 32-year-old Arilen Ndoci, following a suspected burglary at Anmer Hall in Norfolk. The property serves as the country residence for the Prince and Princess of Wales. Police were initially notified of suspicious activity occurring within the broader Sandringham estate, leading to the arrest of the two men. Following the investigation, both individuals, who are noted as being Albanian nationals, were formally charged with burglary and trespass. The pair is expected to appear before the Norwich Magistrates’ Court on Wednesday to address these allegations. The incident has drawn significant media attention due to the high-profile nature of the residence involved in the security breach.",
